5.3 Session Hijacking
Definition: Session hijacking is an attack in which an attacker steals or predicts a valid session identifier and uses it to impersonate an authenticated user.

How it works:

User logs into a website.

Server creates a session ID.

Attacker steals or guesses the session ID.

Attacker uses it to access the victim's session.

Example: An attacker steals a session cookie and gains access to a logged-in account.

