6.12 Advanced forensic concepts your professor may ask
A. Write Blocker
Definition: A write blocker is a hardware or software tool that prevents modification of the original storage device during forensic examination.

Purpose: To preserve original evidence.

B. Forensic Imaging
Definition: Forensic imaging is the process of creating an exact bit-by-bit copy of a storage device for investigation.

Important: Investigators should examine the forensic copy rather than directly modifying the original device.

C. Order of Volatility
Definition: Order of volatility means collecting evidence according to how quickly it can disappear or change.

Typical order:

CPU registers and cache.

RAM and running processes.

Network connections and temporary state.

Disk data.

Backups and archived information.

Q. Why collect RAM before disk data?

A: RAM is volatile. Its contents can disappear when the system loses power.

